0..69 Comment "//! Allocation permutation [Sterling-2023-univalent_reference_types],"
70..149 Comment "//! Fig. 2: two allocations commute. A structure whose parts name each other by"
150..229 Comment "//! ids into an arena is built twice, its nodes allocated in two orders, so the"
230..310 Comment "//! ids of one arena are a relabelling of the other\'s. The relabelling is a path"
311..386 Comment "//! between the id types; the links and the labels carried along it are the"
387..462 Comment "//! other arena\'s, so the two arenas are one, and a consumer that walks the"
463..490 Comment "//! links reads both alike."
491..494 Comment "//!"
495..549 Comment "//! - cites: [Sterling-2023-univalent_reference_types]"
550..553 Comment "//!"
554..711 Comment "//! [Sterling-2023-univalent_reference_types]: https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.CSL.2024.19 \"Sterling, Gratzer and Birkedal, Towards univalent reference types\""
